(664675, 69465, 18194, '<td valign="top">A lot of photos out of car windows in this challenge.  I would have like to have seen back further in the review mirror, this is a bit of a nit I know.  For the most part the photo is very clean and well done the next comments are really for very minor things that I would not have noticed except the rest of the photo is so clean. It looks like there was some cloning going on in the upper left, the train looks just a bit off on the top and the clouds have an odd repeating pattern just left of the tree. At that same point below the tracks seem to have a kink in them.  Around the rear view mirror the edges look a little off as well, kind of rough.  Over all I liked it.</td>', 'A lot of photos out of car windows in this challenge.  I would have like to have seen back further in the review mirror, this is a bit of a nit I know.  For the most part the photo is very clean and well done the next comments are really for very minor things that I would not have noticed except the rest of the photo is so clean. It looks like there was some cloning going on in the upper left, the train looks just a bit off on the top and the clouds have an odd repeating pattern just left of the tree. At that same point below the tracks seem to have a kink in them.  Around the rear view mirror the edges look a little off as well, kind of rough.  Over all I liked it.', '2004-04-12 21:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(664682, 69677, 18194, '<td valign="top">I like the composition of this photo but it is not so good technically.  I realize that you where probably shooting in low light but the focus is off and there is a lot of noise.  I think this could have been improved some by simply de-saturating the photo some.</td>', 'I like the composition of this photo but it is not so good technically.  I realize that you where probably shooting in low light but the focus is off and there is a lot of noise.  I think this could have been improved some by simply de-saturating the photo some.', '2004-04-12 21:27:04.000000', NULL, 1),
