(675173, 69257, 16126, '<td valign="top">This was one of my interest, I''m surprised it didn''t end up higher.</td>', 'This was one of my interest, I''m surprised it didn''t end up higher.', '2004-04-19 08:36:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(675202, 68820, 18216, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the useful comments.<br/> <br/>Live and learn, if people have a hard time identifying the picture...<br/> <br/>This really is a old abandoned dairy building that had a fire. The entire second story was burned away. ( that''s why you can see sky through the ceiling joists.) At this angle, you can''t see the metal fixtures that the cows were behind, but my focus was the trees growing inside the building.</td>', 'Thanks for the useful comments. Live and learn, if people have a hard time identifying the picture... This really is a old abandoned dairy building that had a fire. The entire second story was burned away. ( that''s why you can see sky through the ceiling joists.) At this angle, you can''t see the metal fixtures that the cows were behind, but my focus was the trees growing inside the building.', '2004-04-19 09:00:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(675211, 69506, 16862, '<td valign="top">I´m sorry but I don´t see what is so great about this photo, I feel it´s out of focus, and just low quality in some way. I also think the contrast is not right. And the frame doesn´t look real to me.<br/> <br/>Maybe I´m just blind to the beauty of this picture, but I feel It´s highly overrated. <br/> <br/>Sorry for my negativity, just my opinion<br/> <br/>No disrespect ment</td>', 'I´m sorry but I don´t see what is so great about this photo, I feel it´s out of focus, and just low quality in some way. I also think the contrast is not right. And the frame doesn´t look real to me. Maybe I´m just blind to the beauty of this picture, but I feel It´s highly overrated.  Sorry for my negativity, just my opinion No disrespect ment', '2004-04-19 09:06:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(675219, 69506, 19668, '<td valign="top">It''s a fine picture. I gave it a 9.<br/>But when it got a ribbon a took a closer look and saw that it was staged with a carrie along window frame... ahh... Downgrade in my book.<br/>Hint: Look at the top of the picture. <br/></td>', 'It''s a fine picture. I gave it a 9.But when it got a ribbon a took a closer look and saw that it was staged with a carrie along window frame... ahh... Downgrade in my book.Hint: Look at the top of the picture. ', '2004-04-19 09:26:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(675374, 69111, 18433, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone that commented.  <br/> <br/>BTW this is not a reflection shot, the wall is a long sound barrier with lots of diffrent windows, I selected these due to the contrast of wall and background and the eye-leading lines in it and more.  I had to shoot quite a few ones due to the heavy traffic that kept blocking the view.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone that commented.   BTW this is not a reflection shot, the wall is a long sound barrier with lots of diffrent windows, I selected these due to the contrast of wall and background and the eye-leading lines in it and more.  I had to shoot quite a few ones due to the heavy traffic that kept blocking the view.', '2004-04-19 11:38:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(675409, 69506, 16126, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nicoledb:</b></div><hr/><i> Capture of the sunrise is great, but the window distracts somewhat. For example, the highest stone with the interestingly shaped edge in the foreground is obscured from view. Not sure how to solve that though, without creating other composition problems. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Since this is was a carry-along frame, why not position it better?</td>', 'Originally posted by nicoledb: Capture of the sunrise is great, but the window distracts somewhat. For example, the highest stone with the interestingly shaped edge in the foreground is obscured from view. Not sure how to solve that though, without creating other composition problems.   Since this is was a carry-along frame, why not position it better?', '2004-04-19 12:03:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(675425, 69506, 18219, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=71005" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/18219/thumb/71005.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/18219/thumb/71005.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/18219/thumb/71005.jpg"/></a> <br/>Thanks for voting me to a third place finish.<br/>I appreciate it very much.<br/>As there is so much controversy surrounding lots of "manipulated" pictures, I thought I would show the original picture.<br/>Especially as someone even suggested that there aren''t any rocks at this particular place.<br/> <br/>I went to Folly Beach on Easter Sunday minutes before sunrise. <br/>I took a window frame with me. <br/>The glass had been removed. <br/>I had a basic idea of the view I wanted, but upon getting to the beach I noticed it was low tide and there was a rock pool. <br/>I sat the window frame down in front of the pool and took several shots. <br/>This one was the clearest. <br/>All I did to the picture was crop it. <br/>That''s all. <br/>Absolutely nothing else. <br/>No color or contrast changes. <br/>Judging by some comments, maybe I should have done. <br/>So there you have it. <br/>I bet you don''t get many pictures in the challenges that have so little work done on them? <br/>Maybe the rules need to be changed to allow no manipulation what so ever? <br/>It will stop all the arguments at least! <br/>Or how about that when people submit their entry, they are required to submit the original as well? <br/>That way, the SC people will be able to determine the authenticity of the picture straight away and act accordingly?<br/> <br/>Edit-spelling<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-19 11:27:46.</i></td>', ' Thanks for voting me to a third place finish.I appreciate it very much.As there is so much controversy surrounding lots of "manipulated" pictures, I thought I would show the original picture.Especially as someone even suggested that there aren''t any rocks at this particular place. I went to Folly Beach on Easter Sunday minutes before sunrise. I took a window frame with me. The glass had been removed. I had a basic idea of the view I wanted, but upon getting to the beach I noticed it was low tide and there was a rock pool. I sat the window frame down in front of the pool and took several shots. This one was the clearest. All I did to the picture was crop it. That''s all. Absolutely nothing else. No color or contrast changes. Judging by some comments, maybe I should have done. So there you have it. I bet you don''t get many pictures in the challenges that have so little work done on them? Maybe the rules need to be changed to allow no manipulation what so ever? It will stop all the arguments at least! Or how about that when people submit their entry, they are required to submit the original as well? That way, the SC people will be able to determine the authenticity of the picture straight away and act accordingly? Edit-spelling', '2004-04-19 12:11:59.000000', '2004-04-19 12:27:46.000000', 0),
(675573, 68948, 14891, '<td valign="top">The lighting was from Malibu spot/landscape lights that were aiming up onto my house. They created a really neat shadow with the cross partitions that are in the window. As I took the photo I never even realized they were there, I only tried to focus on the moon, but it was difficult to do because it was also foggy outside. The moon kept coming out of focus, but then I realized that it was fog that I was trying to focus on. (Good luck with that) This was the best one that I found out of 30 or so.<br/>Photographed in Camera RAW, processed in Photoshop CS, color temperature 2200, crop &amp; frame. Voila'' thanks to all that voted/commented. Jason</td>', 'The lighting was from Malibu spot/landscape lights that were aiming up onto my house. They created a really neat shadow with the cross partitions that are in the window. As I took the photo I never even realized they were there, I only tried to focus on the moon, but it was difficult to do because it was also foggy outside. The moon kept coming out of focus, but then I realized that it was fog that I was trying to focus on. (Good luck with that) This was the best one that I found out of 30 or so.Photographed in Camera RAW, processed in Photoshop CS, color temperature 2200, crop & frame. Voila'' thanks to all that voted/commented. Jason', '2004-04-19 13:34:57.000000', NULL, 0),
