(675988, 69678, 1368, '<td valign="top">Wow I have a ribbon!?! Oh my, thanks guys :D Didnt think it would score this high :o  *smile* And thanks for your comments :-)</td>', 'Wow I have a ribbon!?! Oh my, thanks guys :D Didnt think it would score this high :o  *smile* And thanks for your comments :-)', '2004-04-19 16:21:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(676066, 69540, 15207, '<td valign="top">THis is no offence to the people who did get a ribbon, but I''m shocked that this one didn''t edge in just high enough for one. Congrats on the high placement though. Well deserved!</td>', 'THis is no offence to the people who did get a ribbon, but I''m shocked that this one didn''t edge in just high enough for one. Congrats on the high placement though. Well deserved!', '2004-04-19 16:50:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(676096, 69671, 19668, '<td valign="top">When I first saw this picture I was not sure it was real. Still gave it +8. Being a motorcycle rider myself I know things fly by at this kind of speed.<br/>Now when I know what shutter speed was used I did a little math. After a fast calculation I found that your Honda Varadero moved about 15 cm during the exposure. That seems to match the small motion blur seen on the right side of the picture.<br/> <br/>Always remember to ride safe.<br/>Rubber side down! :-)</td>', 'When I first saw this picture I was not sure it was real. Still gave it +8. Being a motorcycle rider myself I know things fly by at this kind of speed.Now when I know what shutter speed was used I did a little math. After a fast calculation I found that your Honda Varadero moved about 15 cm during the exposure. That seems to match the small motion blur seen on the right side of the picture. Always remember to ride safe.Rubber side down! :-)', '2004-04-19 17:06:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(676130, 69658, 12131, '<td valign="top">I think this shot should have scored higher.  Not much to be done now but I like the mistiness of it, combined with the serenity.  Granted the mirror at the bottom is a tad distracting, but that along with the slight reflection on the glass are necessary to show it''s through a window. If anything, maybe soften the edges of the trees a bit. Great shot in my opinion.</td>', 'I think this shot should have scored higher.  Not much to be done now but I like the mistiness of it, combined with the serenity.  Granted the mirror at the bottom is a tad distracting, but that along with the slight reflection on the glass are necessary to show it''s through a window. If anything, maybe soften the edges of the trees a bit. Great shot in my opinion.', '2004-04-19 17:24:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(676133, 69610, 12131, '<td valign="top">I actually like the effect the blinds had on the image.  It breaks that blaring sunlight and adds some odd texture to the view.  Also the light rays are a nice touch.  I like it.</td>', 'I actually like the effect the blinds had on the image.  It breaks that blaring sunlight and adds some odd texture to the view.  Also the light rays are a nice touch.  I like it.', '2004-04-19 17:27:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(676158, 69678, 5112, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Heida!  I like your picture.</td>', 'Congratulations, Heida!  I like your picture.', '2004-04-19 17:35:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(676201, 69506, 15407, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! Very well done and you have set an excellent example by posting this picture.  I have suggested in forums and in comments left,  that some sort of ''verification or comparison'' of the ''source'' photo should be available to the voters, at least with the advanced editing challenges.  Let the voters determine the intent of the rule with their vote.  In the case of your entry I would have voted it even higher.  I AM aware of the voting guidelines which instruct us to vote entry''s as valid or recommend a DQ,  I''ve become skeptical/cynical regarding the entry''s that are beyond my acceptable level of ''refinement''. I''m going to follow you lead by posting a completely ''ORIGINAL'' copy of my Window View entry. Upon its validation the votes trended upwards. Tim<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-19 16:59:41.</i></td>', 'Congratulations! Very well done and you have set an excellent example by posting this picture.  I have suggested in forums and in comments left,  that some sort of ''verification or comparison'' of the ''source'' photo should be available to the voters, at least with the advanced editing challenges.  Let the voters determine the intent of the rule with their vote.  In the case of your entry I would have voted it even higher.  I AM aware of the voting guidelines which instruct us to vote entry''s as valid or recommend a DQ,  I''ve become skeptical/cynical regarding the entry''s that are beyond my acceptable level of ''refinement''. I''m going to follow you lead by posting a completely ''ORIGINAL'' copy of my Window View entry. Upon its validation the votes trended upwards. Tim', '2004-04-19 17:56:12.000000', '2004-04-19 17:59:41.000000', 0),
